> A quote can start at the beginning of the file.

# Lazy continuation (unchanged)

> Quoted paragraph.
This line is still inside the quote.

This paragraph is outside the quote.

# Whitespace-only blank lines

> The quote ends at the following spaces-only line.
   
This paragraph must not be blue.

> The quote ends at the following tab-only line.
	
This paragraph must not be blue either.

> The quote ends at the following mixed whitespace line.
 	 
This paragraph is also outside the quote.

# Unfinished formatting at a quote boundary

> **Unfinished bold inside the quote.

Outside the quote; unfinished bold must not leak here.

> `Unfinished inline code inside the quote.

Outside the quote; unfinished inline code must not leak here.

# A quote cannot interrupt a paragraph in Pandoc markdown

This paragraph has no blank line before the next line.
> This is still literal paragraph text, not a quote.

> With a blank line before it, this is a quote.

# Quoted blank lines remain inside the quote

> First paragraph.
>
> Second paragraph.

# Nested lazy continuation (unchanged)

> > > A nested quote.
Lazy continuation stays quoted.

# Indentation controls (unchanged)

   > Three spaces still allow a quote.

    > Four spaces make an indented code block.
